# Directories (need /* suffix for zip -x@ to exclude recursively)
.git/*
.github/*
.claude/*
node_modules/*

# Development files
.DS_Store
.gitignore
.distignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.gitkeep
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
composer.json
composer.lock
package.json
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Documentation and scripts
# Kept as a guard, not a description: there is no docs/ or designs/ directory
# here any more. Planning documents and design mockups live in the private
# imagewize.com repo under docs/aludra/ and designs/aludra/ (see CLAUDE.md).
# These entries stay so that a stray file re-added here never reaches a zip.
docs/*
designs/
designs/*
bin/*
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md
*.sh
create-pr.sh

# Block tooling. blocks/*/src/* is deliberately NOT excluded: every file under
# blocks/*/build/ is webpack output, and WordPress.org guideline 4 requires the
# human-readable source of compiled JS/CSS to ship alongside it. The src trees
# are ~18k lines / ~1MB, negligible in a zip. The build tooling itself stays
# out — readme.txt's "Building From Source" section documents the commands.
#
# Note the two exclude dialects: create-release.yml uses `zip -x@`, which
# matches whole paths, while plugin-check.yml (and wp-ops rsync-package-to-site)
# use rsync's --exclude-from, where a pattern without a slash matches a basename
# at any depth. That is why the bare `package.json` above also keeps
# blocks/*/package.json out under rsync. Patterns containing a slash, like the
# ones below, are path-anchored in both.
blocks/*/node_modules/*
blocks/*/package.json
blocks/*/package-lock.json
blocks/*/.gitignore
blocks/*/.npmrc
blocks/*/eslint.config.js
blocks/*/.editorconfig

# Temporary files
*.tmp
